From c6eee3d0f20ee5ad50effdade14b371b7057f097 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 01:18:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] build: reject Rust and native compiler warnings

Promote Cargo compiler and rustdoc warnings to errors, including target
and execution-platform Rust actions under Bazel. Enable the native
warnings-as-errors feature for target and host toolchains. Supply that
feature in hermetic LLVM with fatal linker diagnostics, while native
MSVC toolchains use the existing rules_cc feature and /WX flags.

Add a maintained native warning probe that first builds clean code,
then requires the warning fixture to fail at its compiler diagnostic.

Refs: https://github.com/holdmyspot-com/codex-unleashed/issues/61
Authoring evidence: strict-build-warnings-smF5Al/acceptance.md and
latest-toolchains-MzFT3d under .cat/work/temp. Before enforcement the
warning probe builds successfully; with enforcement it fails at -Werror,
and the clean probe passes. just check-build-warnings passes after the
linker-argument compatibility adaptation tracked by issue #60.

Fresh emitted queue and hosted Windows /WX acceptance remain required.
This patch does not claim all toolchain warning boundaries complete.
